SWEET BATTERY (patch 0148, plan step C4): READ-ONLY MAX77759 fuel-gauge reader over HSI2C12 from inside XNU (oriole). Inert unless boot-arg
sweetbatt=1 AND the ADT node /sweet-batt (tools/mkadt.py, only boards whose board.json has an fg block): without both, nothing is mapped and
nothing is read. bsd/dev/sweet_hsi2c_fg.h = the pure port of the reviewed shim --fg-read (branch wip/shim-fg-read, shim/fgread.c at 33304b6,
docs/reviews/fgread-review-fable-1.md: SAFE after F1-F4; observed in run oriole-fg1): all bus access through struct sfg_ops, every store through
sfg_w32() behind sfg_w32_allowed() (the shim's seven writable registers, values and order), the shim's preconditions + the bootloader handoff
words observed in runs oriole-peri1/oriole-fg1, bounded waits, the F1-F3 restore with read-back. Device allowlist {0x36}; register pointers
0x06 0x08 0x09 0x0A 0x0B 0x35 0x21 only (two more than the shim: Current, DevName). bsd/dev/sweet_hsi2c.c = ADT/mapping glue and a kernel
thread (first set 20 s after sweet_ufs_init, then every 30 s; the first refusal or failure stops it for the boot). Output lines
"SWEET BATTERY: ...". Host test: shim/hsi2c_fg_xnu_host_test.c; audit: tools/test_hsi2c_fg_audit.py. BUILT, UNRUN, awaiting an independent
review (different model family) before any hardware run.

